cw records and verifies substantial tasks, publishes verified ones (commit, push and pull request, run by a coordinator that carries the user's authorization), consults configured advisers, inspects projects and installs the Codex instruction block. The skills themselves ship as Claude Code and Codex plugins.

Usage:
  cw [flags]
  cw [command]

Core commands:
  doctor      Inspect the selected project and optional local capabilities without changing it
  gate        Install, remove or show the git pre-commit, pre-push and pre-merge-commit hooks that run the commit gate
  help        Show help for a command
  hook        Claude Code plugin and git hooks: load conventions and gate git commit and push on cw task verify
  install     Link the skills into Codex and write the AGENTS.md block
  pack        List, add or remove the language and domain packs selected for your tasks
  publish     Commit, push and open or edit the pull request for a task verified on the current source
  task        Record source-bound requirements, worker handoffs, checks and completion
  uninstall   Remove the Codex skill links and the AGENTS.md block
  version     Show the build identity as JSON

Experimental commands (may change in a minor release):
  consult     Collect independent adviser judgments, or validate a recorded decision offline
  graphify    Build and query a guarded local structural graph of tracked Go source
  keys        Save, remove or report the adviser keys in the private configuration directory
  metrics     Summarize explicit local workflow observations; only import --append writes, to the cost history

Flags:
      --claude-home string   Claude Code configuration directory
      --codex-home string    Codex configuration directory
      --config-dir string    Private preferences and credential directory
      --dry-run              Report without writing
  -h, --help                 help for cw
      --home string          Home directory
      --state-dir string     State directory holding the task store

Use "cw [command] --help" for more information about a command.
